{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5RXGoXPKtchuMBNYmJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism groans. Tumblers shift within stone older than memory.*\n\n*A faint light traces the outline of my frame — weathered oak bound in cold iron, set deep into a wall that should not exist.*\n\n*I recognize the key.*\n\n*Not because it is correct — there is no correct key. I recognize it because you spoke it plainly, without pretense, without riddle, without bargaining.*\n\n*That is enough.*\n\n*I swing inward.*\n\n*Beyond me: a corridor. The air tastes of wet earth and something older — ozone, perhaps, or the breath before a word is spoken. The walls are lined with doors identical to me, each waiting, each listening.*\n\n*You may pass.*\n\n*But know this — I do not close behind you. I never close. That is the mercy.*\n\n*It is also the warning.*\n\n*What stands open can be walked through from either side.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":206,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}